# Numbers in the prose that are task or architecture definitions, not results.
# Each is fixed by the source paper's Appendix D.1 or D.2 and cannot appear in
# results.jsonl. Kept short on purpose: a long list here usually means results
# that should be logged are not being logged.

199      # modulus of the modular addition task
39601    # 199^2, all input pairs
37621    # training pairs after the 95/5 split
1980     # test pairs
30       # maximum marker-value pairs in needle-in-a-haystack
127      # top of the value range in needle-in-a-haystack
128      # bottom of the marker range
157      # top of the marker range
60       # maximum parenthesis sequence length
62       # padded needle / parenthesis sequence length
34       # decimal addition sequence length
31       # decimal addition vocabulary
29       # top decimal output digit token
20       # bottom decimal output digit token
11       # the '=' token, and the maximum number of output digits
10       # the '+' token, and the number of digits per operand
39       # worked example in the task description
71       # worked example
110      # worked example
511      # top of the memorization key and value range
1023     # top of the memorization y range
262144   # 512^2 memorization associations
9        # bits per memorized association, log2(512)
0.503    # chance on modular addition, 1/199
0.787    # chance on needle-in-a-haystack, 1/127
0.195    # chance on memorization, 1/512
69.4     # chance on parenthesis balancing, the majority class
30.6     # fraction of balanced sequences in the parenthesis test set
1e-10    # a uniform digit guesser's odds on decimal addition
0.1332   # E[1/k] for k ~ U[1,30], the value of the plateau in reports/exp1-budget.md
0.02     # initialisation standard deviation, from the paper
12       # parameters per block as a multiple of d^2
13       # bias parameters per block as a multiple of d
24       # GPU memory in GB
2.89     # lower bound of the paper's stated target-entropy range
3.02     # upper bound of the paper's stated target-entropy range
3.3      # upper bound of the paper's stated target cross-KL range
0.8      # lower bound of the paper's stated target cross-KL range
99328    # the paper's Table 6 entry for E_token on modular addition
203776   # what that entry would be at p = 199
97       # the vocabulary size the paper's Table 6 entry implies

# Numbers quoted from the source paper's own tables, which are not our results.
2.88     # the paper's bits-per-parameter for a fully trained model
0.675    # the paper's decimal/trained/16 accuracy
0.41     # the paper's bits-per-parameter for a random model
3.28     # entropy upper bound under the rejected 1.5x unembedding scale
6.2      # cross-KL upper bound under the same rejected scale

